C03: the pasted file name is the person's text, not machine vocabulary, in the bare-path clarification (FILES1589)

FILES1587 measured that the pasted path was read as the input kind bare_path, but every composed question was refused by the mind's own validity check: `visible_text_leaks_internal_vocabulary` reads a dotted file name («ROADMAP.md», «informe final.docx») as an operation identifier, so both attempts raised and the turns fell to the total-recovery fallback. For that kind the check now runs on the question with the pasted file name removed; the rest of the question is still watched, and the App's policy already exempts identifiers the person supplied.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


